# determinism-topo-tie — a determinism vector over a pipe graph WITH a
# topological tie. A fans out to B, C and E; none of B, C, E pipes to
# another; all three fan in to D, which egresses. The pipe relation admits
# six topological orders (A, then any order of B, C, E, then D). a holds no
# grant at C, so C is refused; D's effective verdict is the join of its own
# auto with B's auto, C's refused and E's auto -> refused; the master
# withholds. SPEC §7.5 pins three things a runner checks here:
#   rule 1 — repeating the activation against this file yields the same
#            verdicts, decision and log every time;
#   rule 2 — every permutation in transport.json yields the same per-gate
#            verdicts and master decision as this file;
#   rule 3 — because the graph has a tie, the log is NOT invariant under
#            reordering: for each file it is the log the §7.4 declaration-order
#            tie-break fixes for that file's gate order. Here B, C, E are
#            declared in that order, so the log runs A, B, C, E, D.
actor a
gate  A grant a
gate  B grant a
gate  C
gate  E grant a
gate  D grant a
cord a -> A
cord A -> B
cord A -> C
cord A -> E
cord B -> D
cord C -> D
cord E -> D
cord D -> master
